Subject: [PATCH] cdev: use vm_flags_set() on RHEL 9 kernels that backported const vm_flags

Building the master on Rocky/RHEL 9.4+ fails with:

    master/cdev.c:233:19: error: assignment of read-only member 'vm_flags'
      233 |     vma->vm_flags |= VM_DONTDUMP;

Mainline Linux 6.3 made vm_area_struct.vm_flags read-only and added the
vm_flags_set()/vm_flags_clear() helpers.  Upstream cdev.c already handles
that, but guards it purely on LINUX_VERSION_CODE:

    #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 3, 0)

Red Hat backported the change into their 5.14 kernel while keeping the
version number frozen for kABI stability.  So on el9 the version test says
"older than 6.3" and selects the direct assignment, while the kernel it is
compiling against has already made the member const.  The version numbers
agree; the code does not.

Extend the guard with a RHEL_RELEASE_CODE test.  This mirrors how upstream
already handles the identical situation for SUSE in devices/generic.c:265:

    #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(5, 15, 0) \
        || (SUSE_VERSION == 15 && SUSE_PATCHLEVEL >= 5)

RHEL_RELEASE_CODE and RHEL_RELEASE_VERSION() come from <linux/version.h> on
RHEL and its derivatives, and are simply absent elsewhere -- hence the
defined() guard, which keeps the expression valid on non-RHEL kernels.

The 9.4 threshold is the point from which this has been observed to be
required; verify on the target with:

    grep -E 'RHEL_MAJOR|RHEL_MINOR|RHEL_RELEASE_CODE' \
         /usr/src/kernels/$(uname -r)/include/linux/version.h
    grep -c 'vm_flags_set' /usr/src/kernels/$(uname -r)/include/linux/mm.h

A non-zero second count means the kernel has the helpers and this patch is
needed.  Adjust the minor version if you meet an older el9 that disagrees.

Applies to: IgH EtherCAT master, tag 1.6.12
Verified on: Rocky 9.8, kernel 5.14.0-687.10.1.el9_8.0.1.x86_64
Not fixed upstream as of stable-1.6 (650888c5); upstream carries no RHEL
guards anywhere in the tree.
---
 master/cdev.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/master/cdev.c b/master/cdev.c
--- a/master/cdev.c
+++ b/master/cdev.c
@@ -227,7 +227,9 @@
     EC_MASTER_DBG(priv->cdev->master, 1, "mmap()\n");

     vma->vm_ops = &eccdev_vm_ops;
-#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 3, 0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 3, 0) \
+    || (defined(RHEL_RELEASE_CODE) \
+        && RHEL_RELEASE_CODE >= RHEL_RELEASE_VERSION(9, 4))
     vm_flags_set(vma, VM_DONTDUMP);
 #else
     vma->vm_flags |= VM_DONTDUMP; /* Pages will not be swapped out */
